WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:04.709
When choosing a premium laptop, you’ve generally
got a choice between a Windows machine, and

00:00:04.709 --> 00:00:09.670
a MacBook, with Windows laptops usually offering
more performance and features at a lower price

00:00:09.670 --> 00:00:13.089
point, and that’s the case for Huawei’s
MateBook X Pro.

00:00:13.089 --> 00:00:21.330
With a quad-core processor, 16GB of RAM, a
3K touchscreen display, 512GB of NVMe SSD

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:27.040
storage, full-speed Thunderbolt 3 and a dedicated
graphics chip, you truly get a lot for your

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:28.040
$1500.

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:34.089
And it’s constantly on sale for just $1300,
and that’s why we’re comparing it to Apple’s

00:00:34.089 --> 00:00:39.969
$1300 2017 13” MacBook Pro, which is constantly
on sale for around $1200.

00:00:39.969 --> 00:00:43.050
We’ve got links to those sales in the description
below.

00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:47.149
We’re gonna be comparing everything we can
between these two laptops, but we’ll focus

00:00:47.149 --> 00:00:53.199
on things that affect your day-to-day experience,
like the display, keyboard, trackpad, speakers

00:00:53.199 --> 00:00:55.010
and overall usability.

00:00:55.010 --> 00:00:59.059
By far, the biggest thing that affects your
experience is the operating system, and if

00:00:59.059 --> 00:01:03.289
you like using Windows 10, the MateBook X
Pro is the obvious choice for what you get

00:01:03.289 --> 00:01:04.289
for the money.

00:01:04.289 --> 00:01:08.150
But there’s a big market of people who prefer
macOS, for reasons like better reliability

00:01:08.150 --> 00:01:12.210
and higher resale value, and they’re okay
paying extra cash to get it.

00:01:12.210 --> 00:01:16.090
Now for those who could really go either way,
let’s compare both laptops and see which

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:20.260
laptop is better in each category, starting
with exterior design.

00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:24.970
The MateBook is slightly thicker near the
rear, but longer and thinner near the front.

00:01:24.970 --> 00:01:29.740
They both share a premium aluminum design
which was introduced by Apple many years ago,

00:01:29.740 --> 00:01:35.070
and the undersides look extremely similar,
with cooling vents located away from the bottom,

00:01:35.070 --> 00:01:37.610
so you can use it on your lap without worrying
about overheating.

00:01:37.610 --> 00:01:38.610
It’s already easy to see how many aspects
of the MacBooks design Huawei borrowed for

00:01:38.610 --> 00:01:39.610
the MateBook, but since they’re a Chinese
company, it’s so difficult for Apple to

00:01:39.610 --> 00:01:40.610
sue them that it’s just not worth it, at
least not yet.

00:01:40.610 --> 00:01:41.610
Let us know what you think about this topic
in the comment section below.

00:01:41.610 --> 00:01:42.610
Upon opening both laptops, you can easily
see what I mean.

00:01:42.610 --> 00:01:43.880
The MateBook almost looks like an exact copy
of the MacBook.

00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:47.750
The truth is that it sucks for Apple, but
it’s great for us consumers because the

00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:49.920
design is admittedly great.

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:54.160
With both laptops looking so similar in design,
it’s gonna have to come down to the fine

00:01:54.160 --> 00:01:57.180
details for the MacBook to have a chance of
getting ahead.

00:01:57.180 --> 00:01:59.020
Let’s start with the displays.

00:01:59.020 --> 00:02:03.090
From first glance, the MateBook’s display
looks many times better than the MacBooks.

00:02:03.090 --> 00:02:08.640
The bezels are much thinner, especially at
the top, thanks to the relocation of the webcam,

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:11.340
literally built into a popup key on the keyboard.

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:16.900
The resolution is higher, at 3K instead of
2.5K and what I really like about it is the

00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:23.181
very tall 3:2 aspect ratio, which is even
taller than the Macbooks 16:10 ratio, which

00:02:23.181 --> 00:02:28.040
gives you a lot more vertical screen space
compared to standard 16:9, which matters a

00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:29.719
lot for browsing the web.

00:02:29.719 --> 00:02:34.980
Not only that, but it’s very color accurate
as well, with 100% sRGB coverage, but the

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:41.680
MacBook Pro takes it further with DCI-P3 wide-color
gamut, which covers 25% more color space than

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:42.680
sRGB.

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:47.189
The MateBook also seems to lack contrast,
with blacks looking a little bit grey compared

00:02:47.189 --> 00:02:49.250
to deep blacks on the MacBook.

00:02:49.250 --> 00:02:53.640
Both displays are almost identical in terms
of maximum brightness, but the MateBook’s

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:57.889
display is also a touchscreen, which can be
nice to have, but we noticed that it’s a

00:02:57.889 --> 00:03:02.730
bit more reflective than the MacBook Pro,
which can get a bit annoying in bright conditions.

00:03:02.730 --> 00:03:07.599
However, I still think the MateBook wins out
in the display category for the near-bezelless

00:03:07.599 --> 00:03:11.790
design, and I think it was really clever to
hide the webcam to be able to achieve it,

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:14.700
even though it makes for an unattractive up-the-nose
camera angle.

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:17.659
I personally never use my MacBooks webcam
anyway.

00:03:17.659 --> 00:03:19.440
Now let’s get to the keyboards.

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:21.700
What you’ve heard about the new MacBook
keys is true.

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:24.139
They don’t have very much key travel at
all.

00:03:24.139 --> 00:03:29.230
The MateBook’s keys remind me of how MacBooks
used to be, with substantially more key travel.

00:03:29.230 --> 00:03:33.200
It honestly just feels better to type on the
MateBook, and you don’t have to worry about

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:36.980
the dead key problem that MacBook’s have
been having, which I personally haven’t

00:03:36.980 --> 00:03:40.549
experienced yet on any of the new MacBooks
I’ve used, so I think it’s a pretty rare

00:03:40.549 --> 00:03:41.549
problem.

00:03:41.549 --> 00:03:45.459
The MateBook’s power button doubles as a
fingerprint reader, which this model of the

00:03:45.459 --> 00:03:46.730
MacBook Pro lacks.

00:03:46.730 --> 00:03:51.889
To get Touch ID, you’ll need to opt for
the more expensive Touch Bar model or a 2018

00:03:51.889 --> 00:03:52.889
MacBook Air.

00:03:52.889 --> 00:03:55.180
Before we test the speakers, let’s compare
the trackpads.

00:03:55.180 --> 00:04:00.129
They look really similar, with the Macbook’s
being slightly bigger, but Apple uses Force

00:04:00.129 --> 00:04:05.150
Touch technology, which basically utilizes
a motor beneath the trackpad to simulate a

00:04:05.150 --> 00:04:06.200
click, just like the solid state home button
works on iPhone 7 and 8.

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:10.040
Click pressure is fully customizable, and
you can basically press firmly after clicking

00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:14.980
once to perform additional options, just like
3D Touch on recent iPhones.

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:19.500
The beauty of using this technology is that
you get an even-clicking feel all around the

00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:24.259
trackpad, unlike the MateBook’s trackpad,
which is easy to click near the bottom and

00:04:24.259 --> 00:04:26.150
almost unclickable near the top.

00:04:26.150 --> 00:04:30.449
The MateBook’s trackpad is still better
than most Windows laptops out there, but the

00:04:30.449 --> 00:04:33.050
MacBook easily wins in this category.

00:04:33.050 --> 00:04:51.250
Now let’s compare the speakers, starting
with

00:04:51.250 --> 00:05:04.800
a sound comparison.

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:08.699
The few things I notIced was that the highs
were a lot brighter on the MacBook, making

00:05:08.699 --> 00:05:11.330
it louder overall compared to the MateBook.

00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:15.539
There wasn’t much of a difference in mids
or bass, but the MacBook sounded more clear

00:05:15.539 --> 00:05:19.599
compared to the MateBook, which sounds a bit
flat like the various sound frequencies are

00:05:19.599 --> 00:05:20.979
clashing together.

00:05:20.979 --> 00:05:24.449
So in almost every scenario, the MacBook speakers
sounded better, but not by too much, like

00:05:24.449 --> 00:05:25.449
other windows laptops.

00:05:25.449 --> 00:05:26.770
Now let’s quickly mention the ports.

00:05:26.770 --> 00:05:32.011
Both get two USB-C ports, with both of them
supporting Thunderbolt 3 on the MacBook, and

00:05:32.011 --> 00:05:36.669
just one on the MateBook, which also gets
a USB-A port, which is really convenient for

00:05:36.669 --> 00:05:39.990
using flash drives, and that port is missing
on the MacBook.

00:05:39.990 --> 00:05:43.569
With that said, all that’s left is specs
and performance.

00:05:43.569 --> 00:05:46.280
You simply get so much more for your money
with the MateBook.

00:05:46.280 --> 00:05:49.050
A 4-core processor instead of a 2-core.

00:05:49.050 --> 00:05:51.909
16GB of RAM compared to 8.

00:05:51.909 --> 00:05:57.020
512GB of SSD storage compared to only 128GB
of the base MacBook Pro, which is actually

00:05:57.020 --> 00:05:58.020
a really huge deal.

00:05:58.020 --> 00:06:03.819
We recommend MacBook users to get at least
256GB, which brings the price up to $1500,

00:06:03.819 --> 00:06:08.840
and if you’re paying that much, you might
as well pay $300 more for the 2018 Touch Bar

00:06:08.840 --> 00:06:09.880
model instead.

00:06:09.880 --> 00:06:14.230
Now the biggest difference is that the MateBook
actually gets dedicated graphics, which you

00:06:14.230 --> 00:06:19.960
can’t get on the MacBook Pro unless you
opt for the 15” model which starts at $2400.

00:06:19.960 --> 00:06:23.689
This was really surprising to us and it puts
the MateBook a step ahead.

00:06:23.689 --> 00:06:28.500
Comparing Geekbench 4 graphics scores, the
difference in graphics performance is significant.

00:06:28.500 --> 00:06:33.199
The quad-core processor also destroys the
dual-core on the MacBook Pro, especially in

00:06:33.199 --> 00:06:36.110
the real-world Cinebench R15 CPU test.

00:06:36.110 --> 00:06:37.479
So what’s the rundown?

00:06:37.479 --> 00:06:39.110
Which laptop is the better choice?

00:06:39.110 --> 00:06:44.120
Well, if you don’t mind using Windows, the
2019 MateBook X Pro is by far the better machine

00:06:44.120 --> 00:06:45.120
to buy for your money.

00:06:45.120 --> 00:06:48.979
There are ways the MacBook Pro is definitely
better, but it’s not nearly enough to top

00:06:48.979 --> 00:06:50.280
the value of the MateBook.

00:06:50.280 --> 00:06:54.500
And the best part is that it looks and feels
pretty similar to the MacBook, with a much

00:06:54.500 --> 00:06:56.160
better keyboard and display.

00:06:56.160 --> 00:07:01.150
Now if you own an iPhone, Apple Watch, maybe
an iPad or a set of AirPods, you’re going

00:07:01.150 --> 00:07:05.000
to have a much better experience with the
MacBook Pro with all of the features you get

00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:06.000
with the Apple ecosystem.

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:11.169
And MacBooks generally tend to be more reliable
and age better compared to Windows laptops,

00:07:11.169 --> 00:07:15.250
so that’s another factor to consider if
you plan on keeping your laptop for many years.

00:07:15.250 --> 00:07:19.259
But for the sake of comparing the value of
these two laptops, the MateBook wins, hands

00:07:19.259 --> 00:07:20.259
down.

00:07:20.259 --> 00:07:21.259
No doubt at all.

00:07:21.259 --> 00:07:22.259
No competition.

00:07:22.259 --> 00:07:23.620
If you enjoyed this comparison, make sure
to hit that subscribe button, because we’re

00:07:23.620 --> 00:07:27.699
getting our hands on the 2019 iMac really
soon and we’ll be doing comparison videos

00:07:27.699 --> 00:07:28.699
on that as well.

00:07:28.699 --> 00:07:34.139
Thanks for watching, and we’ll see you in
the next video.

